reeting Salam  comes from the Arabic word Salam meaning  peace the word for thank you  the Shaq kiram comes from the Arabic  word meaning thankful with the shockula  with the person conjugation meaning I am  jadeed meaning knew a moment ago we saw  the indo-european word no meaning new  this is an alternate word many Arabic  borrowings also have native Persian  equivalents that's meaning lesson or  course from the Arabic noun meaning  lesson there are many Arabic words in  Persian but the percentage of Arabic  words depends on the formality and style  of speech or writing pronunciation the  pronunciation of Persian is not too  complicated  most of the consonant sounds are sounds  that appear in English but the following  consonants are worth noting huh  this is like the consonant at the end of  Scottish law Northcote an O in Iranian  Persian today these are both mainly the  same sound which is a voiced equivalent  of a a consonant which exists in Arabic  oh yeah um traditionally these were  different sounds and then that was  pronounced ha but the two sounds have  mostly merged this is like the French je  sound yeah it mainly appears in  loanwords you on ha the Persian Rohtak  sound is normally an alveolar tap more  than it also appears as a short alveolar  trill though that seems inconsistent and  depends on the speaker tongue dad there  are six basic vowel sounds 3 short and 3  long short ah  Oh long e the long vowels are pronounced  longer and are represented by abjad  characters in writing and as I mentioned  before the short vowels are only  indicated with diacritics which are not  normally written notice that the to a  sounds are not only different in length  but also quality the long vowel is more  of an open back vowel ah while the short  version is an open front vowel ah stress  usually occurs on the last syllable of  words then done but this is not always  the case with verbs because the stress  moves depending on the presence of  certain particles or affi